# Treat Quack source (.sta) as Verilog for GitHub syntax highlighting and language stats.
# Quack is a Verilog-like HDL (modules, ports, wires, instances), so Verilog's highlighter is the
# closest match GitHub (Linguist) offers. It will not know Quack-specific tokens like `<|`, `inf`,
# or `min`, but colors keywords, comments, and numbers far better than plain text.
# (GitHub cannot use a custom per-repo grammar; it only highlights languages in its Linguist set.)
*.sta linguist-language=Verilog

# Keep the .sta files out of the language-stats breakdown being dominated by generated/sample code
# is not a concern here, but mark them as documentation-adjacent sample sources if desired:
# *.sta linguist-detectable=true

# Normalize line endings so the repo is consistent across OSes (silences CRLF warnings).
* text=auto eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.hpp text eol=lf